  import os, sys, torch; R = os.environ["R"]
  sys.path.insert(0, f"{R}/scripts/flash_v2")
  import hybrid_v2 as HB      # puts $R/src/flashTP-cgpatch at sys.path[0] and asserts flashTP_e3nn.__file__ is there
  M = f"{R}/models/MACE-OFF23_medium.model"
  # 1. e3nn reference (fp64)
  calc, info = HB.build_calc(M, conv="e3nn", sc="e3nn")
  # 2. FlashTP-FP64CG (FlashTP conv_tp+scatter, e3nn SymmetricContraction)
  calc, info = HB.build_calc(M, conv="flashtp", sc="e3nn")
  # 3. cueq (stock MACE)
  from mace.calculators import MACECalculator
  calc = MACECalculator(model_paths=M, device="cuda", default_dtype="float64", compute_stress=False, enable_cueq=True)
  # 4. hybrid (FlashTP conv + cuEquivariance SymmetricContraction)
  calc, info = HB.build_calc(M, conv="flashtp", sc="cueq")
  model = calc.models[0]   # info["backend_map"], info["flash_cg"], info["cueq_sc"]

Notes:
- build_calc never changes torch's global default dtype and works under either default. The dtype argument sets the model and FlashTP dtype.
- At build time it asserts that the FlashTP CG table is fp64, contains values not representable in fp32, and matches e3nn's fp64 wigner_3j to within 1e-14 (measured 7e-16).
- Zero-edge graphs (single atom, all atoms > r_max apart, batches with E=0) return zeros without launching the kernel. Forces are 0 and energies equal e3nn's.
- check_indices=True adds one aminmax and one host sync per layer per call. Pass build_calc(..., check_indices=False) for timing runs; for those runs, report which setting you used.
- Use one calc/model per thread and stream. TorchScript, torch.compile and LAMMPS are not supported.
- While FlashTP is installed, torch.save(model) and deepcopy(model) raise AdapterError. model.state_dict() is safe and returns the stock keys.
- FA = HB.FA; FA.uninstall(model) is idempotent.
- Parity vs e3nn, worst case over 3 geometries x {H2O, water192, water648} x both defaults, for both flash and hybrid:
  |dE|/atom <= 1.5e-13 eV; max|dF| <= 7.1e-15 eV/A; RMS|dF| <= 1.2e-15 eV/A.
  Repeat variation on the same geometry was 0 for all backends in these runs. That is not guaranteed: the kernels use atomics.
